From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] addons: enable the web apps repository on first start

Kodi registers an add-on it finds for the first time as disabled unless
the add-on manifest names it. The kodi-addon-repository-webapps package
installs repository.dangowrt.webapps next to Kodi's own add-ons, so a
fresh installation came up with the web apps repository switched off.
Listing it as an optional system add-on enables it on first start and
leaves the user free to disable it; on an installation without the
package the entry has no effect.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 system/addon-manifest.xml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/system/addon-manifest.xml
+++ b/system/addon-manifest.xml
@@ -57,5 +57,6 @@
   <addon optional="true">game.shader.presets</addon>
   <addon optional="true">inputstream.adaptive</addon>
   <addon optional="true">peripheral.joystick</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">repository.dangowrt.webapps</addon>
   <addon optional="true">service.xbmc.versioncheck</addon>
 </addons>
